   * rotation, in the order listed. A session opened with a later password is
   * resealed with the first one, so the rotation moves forward as users make
   * requests. Order matters: an older password placed first would seal new
   * sessions. Removing a password from the list invalidates every session sealed
   * with it. Sessions read only from the session header keep their older seal
   * until they expire. Keep the list short (2 or 3): each password costs a PBKDF2
   * derivation per request carrying an unknown cookie.
   *
